    "step": "step:42-2",
    "summary": "Seek's claims no longer go one seeker at a time in contest order. In each of `ROUNDS` (3) rounds, every seeker that isn't placed yet proposes a slot on the pool, against the claims settled in earlier rounds. A proposal wins unless one with a higher contest key lies within a body's breadth of it. Winners aim, in squad and member order. Losers propose again in the next round, and after the last round the rest press toward the nearest slot. - The rule is `src/settling.rs` (`winners`: each proposal's key, point and reach, checked through a grid), so step 3 can reuse it. - `Claims` is a flat grid, `within` is `Fn + Sync`, and `pick` no longer clones a seeker's owned slots. - Round 1 proposes `kept` (the slot a seeker made for, if still open). Later rounds `pick`. Slots found claimed are marked dead between rounds.",
    "title": "feat(native): seek's claims settled in rounds (spec 42 step 2)"
  },
